Here's the refactor, tied finding-by-finding to the crimes output.

## Refactored `src/Card.tsx`

```tsx
import styles from "./Card.module.css";

export function Card({
  children,
  onActivate,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode;
  onActivate: () => void;
}) {
  return (
    <button type="button" className={styles.card} onClick={onActivate}>
      <div className={styles.body}>{children}</div>
      <aside className={styles.sidebar}>sidebar</aside>
    </button>
  );
}
```

## Companion `src/Card.module.css`

```css
.card {
  /* design tokens — no raw hex/rgb in JSX */
  background: var(--color-surface-accent);
  color: var(--color-text-primary);
  border: 1px solid var(--color-border-subtle);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  outline-color: var(--color-focus-ring);

  /* fluid layout — width drives from container, not 800px */
  width: 100%;
  max-width: var(--size-card-max, 64rem);
  padding: var(--space-6);
  display: grid;
  gap: var(--space-4);
  grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  font: inherit;
  text-align: inherit;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.body {
  font-size: clamp(1rem, 0.9rem + 0.4vw, 1.125rem);
}

.sidebar {
  font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
}

/* container query: side-by-side only when there's room */
@container (min-width: 40rem) {
  .card {
    grid-template-columns: 3fr 1fr;
  }
}
```

## Why each change maps to a finding

| Finding | Change | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| **crime_00001 — Accessible Interaction Risk** (`<div onClick>`) | Swap the outer `<div onClick>` for a real `<button type="button">`; rename the prop to `onActivate` so callers can't accidentally re-add a click-only `div`. Keyboard activation, focus ring, and screen-reader semantics come for free — no `role`/`tabIndex`/keydown shim needed. The inner `<div>sidebar</div>` becomes `<aside>` so it's announced correctly. | Finding says "use semantic elements; add ARIA only when semantics don't fit." A button **is** the semantic element here, so we don't reach for `role="button"`. |
| **crime_00002 — Design Token Escape** (9 raw values across color/px/rgb/shadow) | Move all styling into a CSS Module. Every color becomes `var(--color-*)`, the shadow becomes `var(--shadow-sm)`, padding becomes `var(--space-6)`. Zero hex/rgb literals remain in the TSX. | Agents extending the file now see token names, not raw `#ff00aa` — they can't copy a literal forward without first reading the token. The detector triggers on hard-coded values in JSX; routing through `var(...)` removes the trip-wire entirely. |
| **crime_00003 — Responsive Fragility** (`width: 800px`, `width: 720px`, `fontSize: 18`, no `@media`) | Outer card: `width: 100%` + `max-width: var(--size-card-max)` instead of `800px`. Inner body: dropped the `720px` fixed width — grid handles it. Typography: `clamp()` for the body, `var(--font-size-sm)` for the sidebar. Layout collapse handled by a **container query** (`@container (min-width: 40rem)`) rather than a viewport `@media`, so the card responds to its slot, not the window. | Finding's fix shape literally says "drive layout from container queries or a fluid scale, not pixel media queries." `clamp()` + container queries is exactly that. |

## Two judgment calls worth flagging

- **Button vs. anchor.** I assumed this is an in-page action (the original was `console.log`). If activating a card navigates somewhere, swap `<button>` for `<a href>` — same a11y win, different semantics.
- **Container query parent.** `@container` needs an ancestor with `container-type: inline-size`. If the parent layout doesn't already set that, the side-by-side breakpoint silently never fires. Add `container-type: inline-size` to the card's parent, or change `.card` to `container-type: inline-size` and move the grid onto a child wrapper.
